1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:52,000
そっとくれるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の定世 窓辺からやがて到達

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
ほっ飛ばしる熱いパックスで 思い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:42,000
死人の一生

10
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
アトロト

11
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:07,840
There was no other choice!

12
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,700
Because he was an angel!

13
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,180
Koro was an angel!

14
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:14,680
He was still an angel!

15
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,580
He was still one of the enemy!

16
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,500
He wasn't! He wasn't!

17
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:20,680
He wasn't!

18
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,680
Even though he was as human as me?

19
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,820
No! He was an angel!

20
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,060
Is that why you killed him?

21
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,700
Yes! Otherwise we'd all die!

22
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,460
We'd have all been destroyed!

23
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,540
So that's why you killed him?

24
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,180
I didn't want to kill him!

25
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,040
I didn't have a choice!

26
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,380
Help me!

27
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,500
Please, just help me!

28
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,420
For God's sake, help me!

29
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:48,100
I didn't want to kill him!

30
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:48,600
I didn't want to kill him!

31
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:49,660
Is anyone listening?

32
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,100
Somebody please help me!

33
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:58,720
He was much better than I am.

34
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:02,400
Koro should have survived, not me.

35
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:03,020
No!

36
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:08,320
The one who deserves to survive is the one who has the will to make it happen!

37
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,220
He wished for death!

38
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:16,660
He ignored his will to survive and chose to die for a false hope!

39
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,980
Survival is not a mistake, Shinji!

40
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:20,900
Are you sure?

41
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,220
Are you sure it was right?

42
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,720
I don't understand!

43
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,480
What can I do?

44
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,460
What am I supposed to do?

45
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,500
What was that?

46
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,500
I fear myself?

47
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,600
I fear being hated?

48
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:37,760
But by whom?

49
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,080
Who is it?

50
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,040
It's my...

51
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,080
Father.

52
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,480
My father abandoned me!

53
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:44,460
He hates me!

54
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,200
If others hate me, what will I do?

55
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,560
What will I do?

56
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,820
What will I do?

57
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:52,000
What will I do?

58
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,760
What will I do?

59
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,580
Where am I?

60
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,420
Where am I supposed to go?

61
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,020
I can't see anything.

62
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,920
I don't understand what I feel.

63
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:11,580
Misato?

64
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:13,600
Misato!

65
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,320
Hey!

66
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,920
Where are you, Misato?

67
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,000
I can't see!

68
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,680
Hey, where am I supposed to go?

69
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:23,820
Misato!

70
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,140
Asuka!

71
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:26,240
Ainami!

72
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:27,560
Toji!

73
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:28,440
Kitsuke!

74
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,200
Ritsuko!

75
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:29,920
Kaji!

76
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,180
Father!

77
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,140
Mother!

78
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:37,280
Somebody please tell me what I have to do now!

79
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,520
Evangelion Unit 1!

80
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:46,520
I still have to pilot it?

81
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,340
Even after it made me kill him?

82
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:53,720
My father and the others tell me that I have to pilot it no matter what I want!

83
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,340
Why do I have to keep fighting after all that's happened?

84
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:57,160
Mother!

85
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,460
Say something!

86
00:04:59,020 --> 00:04:59,880
Answer me!

87
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:04,200
Because everyone tells me to.

88
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:05,700
Because everyone tells me to.

89
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,320
What do you mean?

90
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:08,060
It's for the sake of mankind.

91
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,640
Isn't that good enough?

92
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,980
That's right!

93
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:14,120
Is there something wrong with that?

94
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:15,960
I'm doing the right thing!

95
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,860
And when I do it, the others appreciate me!

96
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,620
The others like me then!

97
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,660
You're lying!

98
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:22,520
Huh?

99
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:23,980
Are you stupid?

100
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:26,860
You know damn well that you do this for yourself.

101
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:27,720
Huh?

102
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:31,040
You're just making up excuses like you always do.

103
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,140
I do?

104
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:36,300
Pretending you're sacrificing yourself is just another cop-out.

105
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:39,160
It makes you feel so special to play the martyr.

106
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:40,500
I'm not sure that's true.

107
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:43,800
You're feeling lonely and isolated, nothing more.

108
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:44,680
Am I?

109
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,860
Of course you are!

110
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:50,400
You live on sympathy and you get it with your Eva, Shinji!

111
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:51,320
It could be true.

112
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:53,940
You love having others depend upon you.

113
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,820
It satisfies your twisted little mind.

114
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:57,880
It could be.

115
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:05,380
If you want real happiness, you've got to find it for yourself, not wait for someone to give it to you.

116
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,680
But isn't that what you've been doing?

117
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:19,840
Didn't want to be in this thing again.

118
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:22,180
They're forcing me to buy like this.

119
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,240
But this piece of junk won't work.

120
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:28,600
But it's only junk because of what I've become.

121
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,680
I'm the garbage now.

122
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,580
I'm worthless.

123
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:34,640
Nobody needs me.

124
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:39,500
But he needs a pilot who can't even control her own Eva!

125
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,660
You seek your own value in the perception of others.

126
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,080
Shut up!

127
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,620
Do you fear being alone?

128
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:52,200
Do you fear being you afraid that you will lose your identity if others leave you?

129
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:55,120
You pilot Eva so you'll be preyed!

130
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,180
Shut up!

131
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:57,360
Shut up!

132
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,720
Leave me alone!

133
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:02,040
How can a wind-up doll like you dare tell me that?

134
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:06,620
Who am I?

135
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,000
You are Rei Ayanami.

136
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:10,320
But who are you?

137
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:13,860
Are you Rei Ayanami as well?

138
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:14,680
Correct.

139
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,340
I'm the thing that is recognized as Rei Ayanami.

140
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,680
We are all things that are recognized as Rei Ayanami.

141
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:23,080
How could all of those possibly be me?

142
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:26,260
It is simply because the others call us Rei Ayanami.

143
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:27,660
That is the only reason.

144
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:30,580
You possess a false body and a fake soul.

145
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,080
Do you know I?

146
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,080
I am neither false nor fake.

147
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,160
I am simply me.

148
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,160
No.

149
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:41,840
You are an empty shell with a false soul created by a man named Gendo Ikari.

150
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:45,100
You are just an object that is pretending to be a human.

151
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,880
Look deep within yourself.

152
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:52,340
Do you perceive the almost intangible and invisible presence that lurks below your waking self?

153
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:55,180
Inside your darkest dreams, my lord.

154
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,720
It is there that your true identity lies.

155
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,240
No, I am me.

156
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:05,420
I became myself by the instrumentality of the links and relationships between myself and others.

157
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,700
I am formed by interaction with others.

158
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,860
They create me as I create them.

159
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:16,080
These relationships and interactions serve to shape the patterns of my heart and mind.

160
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:22,980
Yes, that is the name for what I share with those who have created the thing known as Rei.

161
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,680
That is what will continue to shape me.

162
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:30,000
But there is someone else who is your true self.

163
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,440
You don't know her, but she exists.

164
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:38,440
You deny that fact and attempt to suppress that facet of your reality.

165
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,720
Because she might not have human form.

166
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:45,480
Because then the present self might cease to be.

167
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:50,200
This is what you fear, that you will become nothing.

168
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:54,780
You are frightened that you will disappear from the minds of others if another exists.

169
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:55,800
I'm afraid.

170
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:57,380
Why is that?

171
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:00,400
Because your current self will have never existed.

172
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:03,380
Because you will cease to be.

173
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:06,780
No, I'm not.

174
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,480
I am happy.

175
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,400
Because I want to die.

176
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:13,420
I want despair.

177
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,360
I want to return to nothing.

178
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,140
But I can't.

179
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,980
He won't let me return to nothingness.

180
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,080
Not yet.

181
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,680
I still exist because he needs me.

182
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:32,640
But when everything is over, when I am of no use anymore, he will abandon me.

183
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:36,000
I've prayed for the day he would abandon me.

184
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:39,720
But now, now I fear it.

185
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:44,340
Come, let us go.

186
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:49,200
This is the day for which you were created, Rey.

187
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,680
Yes, sir.

188
00:09:50,680 --> 00:10:03,120
What?

189
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,060
What feeling is this?

190
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,580
I think I've experienced this sensation before.

191
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:12,140
It's as though my physical form was disappearing.

192
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,760
It feels agreeable.

193
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:19,120
As though my existence is spreading itself out to cover the entirety of existence.

194
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:33,240
Incorrect.

195
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:35,280
It is not a return to nothingness.

196
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:37,960
It is merely a return to a state of beginning.

197
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:42,340
It is no less than a return to the primal womb that we lost so long ago.

198
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:45,960
Souls and minds will become one, attaining eternal balance.

199
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:48,320
The final goal is nothing more than that.

200
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,980
And that's instrumentality.

201
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:50,680
Yes.

202
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:53,560
There is an emptiness at the very core of our souls.

203
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:58,260
A fundamental incompleteness that has haunted all beings since the very first thought.

204
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:03,340
On a primal level, man has always been aware of the darkness that resides at the core of his mind.

205
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,560
We have seeked to escape from this void and the fear it causes.

206
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:09,540
And all man's accomplishments were made in the hope of filling it.

207
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:12,480
And so you'll just crush everyone's minds together to fill the gaps?

208
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,640
Who made you humanity's overseer?

209
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:19,440
You came to us bearing an offer of help, yet your benevolence has proved to be as false as our friendship.

210
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:22,100
And yet that is exactly as you wished it to be.

211
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,000
Where am I?

212
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:31,300
This is the me that exists in your mind, Misato.

213
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:35,300
And yet at the same time, this is also the me which exists in your mind.

214
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,200
Isn't it, Shinji?

215
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:40,960
In order to establish my identity, I have to communicate with the minds of many people.

216
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:43,560
I have to examine that which is at my core.

217
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:47,420
I have to stare at Misato, who resides on the inside of my mind.

218
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,400
What is it that you wish for, Misato?

219
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:52,860
I have to be a good child.

220
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,680
Because I have no daddy.

221
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:58,420
Because I have to be good and not bother my mommy.

222
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,440
But I don't want to become like my mom.

223
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:03,800
When my father is not here, she always cries.

224
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,200
I can't cry.

225
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,240
I can't depend on anyone else.

226
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,720
So I have to be good.

227
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,100
That way maybe my father won't hate me as much.

228
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:12,020
I hope.

229
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:14,600
Maybe my father won't hate me if I be good.

230
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,720
But I hated my father.

231
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:18,200
And I hated being a good child.

232
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,800
I hate it.

233
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:21,820
I'm tired of it.

234
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:24,180
I'm tired of keeping myself clean.

235
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:27,040
I'm tired of pretending to be pure and noble.

236
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,900
I'm so tired of it all.

237
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:32,620
I want to disgrace myself to get so dirty that no one can stand it.

238
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,920
I want to see my life and my reputation ruined.

239
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,620
Is that why you slept with him?

240
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:37,640
With Kaji?

241
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:40,320
No, I slept with him because I love him.

242
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:41,320
You did?

243
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,560
Did you really love him?

244
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:44,580
Yes, I did.

245
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:47,260
He accepted me as myself for the real me.

246
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:50,460
That's why I let him make love to me.

247
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:03,660
No!

248
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,240
Don't show Cindy this.

249
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,000
I don't want him to see that side of me.

250
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:10,460
Why are you still embarrassed after all that's happened?

251
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,580
Because I'm ashamed of it.

252
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:14,240
Why does this embarrass you?

253
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,360
You weren't ashamed then.

254
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,900
You were glad to show your true nature to the man you loved.

255
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,760
In fact, you took great pleasure in it.

256
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:21,260
No, don't do this!

257
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:24,060
You wanted to dirty yourself.

258
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:27,440
You should be happy to show this side of yourself to Shinji, shouldn't you?

259
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:27,880
No!

260
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:29,040
No, no!

261
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:31,000
Are you sure?

262
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:34,060
Or is it perhaps your father that you'd like to show this to?

263
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:34,460
No!

264
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:38,980
Wasn't it really peace of mind that you were seeking in Kaji's bed?

265
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:39,480
No!

266
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:43,160
You wanted peace of mind and warmth from Kaji then?

267
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,000
No!

268
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,980
You wanted to find your father in Kaji's embrace, didn't you?

269
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,240
Is that true?

270
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,640
It is true.

271
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,120
In Kaji, I had found my father reborn.

272
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:55,540
And so I fled from him.

273
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,140
I was so afraid.

274
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,440
He was so much like my father.

275
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,900
But at the same time, I was also very happy.

276
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:05,020
I was never happier.

277
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,820
That was such a wonderful time.

278
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:10,140
That's why I hated it.

279
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,320
That's why I left.

280
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,300
That's why I ran away.

281
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:24,440
So, no reason was required to begin our love, but you needed a reason for ending it.

282
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:27,160
Yes, you were so kind, Kaji.

283
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,460
You were so kind to disgrace me.

284
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,620
To dirty me.

285
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,440
To deflower me.

286
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:41,020
Just because you hate yourself is no reason to injure yourself further.

287
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:45,660
Punishing yourself is simply a cheat to make you feel better for a little while.

288
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,080
Don't do this to yourself.

289
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,640
And now you'll tell me to take care of myself?

290
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:52,980
Men always do that.

291
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:58,080
They'll escape to their jobs, their own world, and leave me behind.

292
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:00,540
They always leave me behind.

293
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:01,740
Always.

294
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,600
Just like our father did.

295
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:07,420
They always escape from the harsh realities.

296
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:09,540
Harsh reality.

297
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:12,300
I am his harsh reality.

298
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:16,760
Of course, I am the problem.

299
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:17,740
Stop this!

300
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:18,600
Misato.

301
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:21,060
Why should anyone else love me anyway?

302
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:22,520
I hate myself!

303
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,720
You're vulgar and impure.

304
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:25,920
You're pathetic.

305
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,040
You're gross and disgusting!

306
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:31,160
I've never seen anyone in such a disgusting relationship!

307
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:35,000
Congratulations on your promotion, Major Katsuragi.

308
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,220
The me who's recognized is the me who's performing a role in order to be appreciated.

309
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,040
But she's not the real me.

310
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,220
Your true self is always crying, isn't she?

311
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:45,680
Yes.

312
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:47,000
But I am happy.

313
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,240
I am happy.

314
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,840
It's true.

315
00:15:52,980 --> 00:15:53,900
I am happy.

316
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:55,720
I'm not.

317
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,720
This isn't the happiness I want.

318
00:15:59,020 --> 00:15:59,880
This isn't me.

319
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:01,300
It is not the true myself.

320
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:03,740
I just don't want to face the harsh reality.

321
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,100
But we have to.

322
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,620
We cannot live otherwise.

323
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,220
You know you'd be alone and afraid.

324
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,520
Unstable.

325
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,980
If nobody was sleeping next to you.

326
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:14,900
Are you afraid of sleeping alone?

327
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:18,160
Or does sleeping by yourself remind you of how empty your life is?

328
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:20,960
She can't stand not having other souls around her.

329
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,300
So you'll sleep with anyone, won't you, Major?

330
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:23,960
No!

331
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,200
Yes, you just want to be infatuated with primal ecstasy.

332
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:31,280
You want to fill the hole in your heart with temporary escape.

333
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:34,560
You take advantage of men to soothe the pain in your soul.

334
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:35,560
No!

335
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,220
No!

336
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:36,900
No!

337
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,160
Where am I?

338
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:47,500
This is the me which exists in your mind, Asuka.

339
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:51,680
And also, this is the me that exists in Shinji's mind at the same time.

340
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:53,460
I can't stop now.

341
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:55,460
What do you want, Asuka?

342
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,840
I want to live by myself.

343
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,620
I don't want my papa and my mama.

344
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,440
I'll live by myself.

345
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:05,640
And then, I won't cry anymore.

346
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:09,980
But I'm still crying.

347
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,560
Why am I crying?

348
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:13,040
I am sorry.

349
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:14,860
I just don't like her.

350
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,740
What happened to you, the able doctor?

351
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:21,800
I told you, I'm a human being before I was old.

352
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,300
But how can a trained person like you?

353
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,060
She acts too much like an adult.

354
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,160
And she rejects me, absolutely.

355
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:31,140
Sometimes, she even scares me.

356
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:33,420
Have you had such a feeling with her?

357
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:34,700
No.

358
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:38,160
And in any case, you have now become Asuka's mother.

359
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:40,620
I'm your wife before that.

360
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:43,120
Both duties are concurrent.

361
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,940
In a social perspective, yes.

362
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,420
But you can't quit being her father.

363
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,560
However, I can quit being her mother anytime.

364
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,040
You can say that.

365
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:58,520
No, mama!

366
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,240
Don't leave me!

367
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,760
I'll be good!

368
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,460
Promise!

369
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:05,200
Don't stop being my mother!

370
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,240
Don't ignore me!

371
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:08,940
No, mama!

372
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:11,120
Don't kill me!

373
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:13,280
Your papa hates your mama.

374
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:15,580
He doesn't need me anymore.

375
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:16,760
No.

376
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:19,080
He didn't love me to begin with.

377
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,240
But let's die together.

378
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,420
Because he doesn't want us.

379
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,680
He didn't need me at all.

380
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:28,540
And he doesn't want you either, Asuka.

381
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:29,540
I'm not wanted!

382
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,720
I'm not worth anything!

383
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:34,400
Die with me, too.

384
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:35,740
No!

385
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,800
I am not your soul!

386
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:40,780
I'll think by myself and live by myself!

387
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:45,120
And then, my mother was hanging from the ceiling.

388
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:48,260
She looked so happy.

389
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:51,360
But I hated how she looked.

390
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,440
I don't want to die.

391
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:55,440
I don't want to disappear.

392
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,820
I hate this.

393
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,800
I hate boys.

394
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:03,040
I hate my father and my mother.

395
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,680
I hate everyone.

396
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:06,980
Nobody cares about me.

397
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:08,760
Nobody stays with me.

398
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:13,400
So I don't want to depend on anybody.

399
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:16,020
But I hate it at the same time.

400
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,540
It's a pain.

401
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:19,840
I don't want to be alone.

402
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:21,660
I don't want to be alone!

403
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:23,100
I don't want to be alone!

404
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,120
Don't leave me.

405
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:27,960
Don't ignore me.

406
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:29,480
Don't kill me!

407
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:33,900
What the hell is this?

408
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:38,880
This is the instrumentality which your father has initiated.

409
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,100
This is it?

410
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,560
This is part of it.

411
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,460
You can't tell what the truth is, Shinji.

412
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:47,540
Truth is subjective.

413
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:51,000
Therefore, you can barely tell that what you can feel is fact.

414
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:52,820
The truth is within you.

415
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:57,700
And the facts that remain in your memory are what will become your truth.

416
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:00,040
Truth can be changed from time to time.

417
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:00,920
Sometimes.

418
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:02,800
This is all fact.

419
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,960
This is the result of everything?

420
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,880
This is real, but one of many realities.

421
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,220
This is the conclusion you wanted.

422
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:11,560
Wanted?

423
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:12,340
Me?

424
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:13,000
Yes.

425
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,220
Total destruction.

426
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:17,320
You wished for a world in which nobody would be saved.

427
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,200
No!

428
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:19,800
I didn't wish for this!

429
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,440
The others didn't save me!

430
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,740
Nobody can save you from yourself.

431
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,440
This is what you wished for.

432
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:29,640
Destruction, death, and return to nothingness.

433
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:31,280
You wished for these.

434
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,760
This is the reality that is.

435
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,300
What is reality?

436
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:36,960
This is your world.

437
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,260
A world that exists solely for yourself.

438
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,480
One without time, space, or anyone else.

439
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:46,400
A world in which every facet is determined by you.

440
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:50,920
This is the world in which you just wait for others to give you something.

441
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:54,780
This is your world unless you decide to change reality.

442
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,260
This is the world that is!

443
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,780
Nothing can change that!

444
00:20:58,020 --> 00:20:58,340
No.

445
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,080
You yourself make the decision.

446
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:03,760
This is the world where your mind decides what will be.

447
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:11,160
Whether it is the will to survive, or a wish for death, it is all up to you.

448
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:17,140
Are you saying that this darkness, this insane world, are what I really wish to create?

449
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:17,680
Yes.

450
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:21,440
You wished for a closed world that was comfortable for you.

451
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:24,680
You wished for it in order to protect you from your wounds.

452
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,280
To protect your few pleasures.

453
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:30,340
This is merely the result of your wish.

454
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:35,000
In your closed world, in a world where only you are allowed to be, others cannot live with you.

455
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,880
But still you wished to close off the world that surrounded you.

456
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:44,660
Your wish ejected things you disliked, and created an isolated and lonely world filled with nothing.

457
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:47,700
This is the world your wishes have created.

458
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,620
A private haven in the recesses of your mind.

459
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:52,980
This is how it all ends.

460
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,680
One of many possible endings.

461
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:57,180
This is an ending you brought upon yourself.

462
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,800
You choose this fate.

463
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,760
You choose this fate.

464
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:30,740
You choose this fate.

465
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,760
to kiss me.

466
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:37,400
And feel my heart with love.

467
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:41,680
But let me sing forever more.

468
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,600
You are all my love.

469
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:48,840
The path is always acceptable.

470
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:52,580
In other ways.

471
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,180
Please be true.

472
00:22:56,180 --> 00:23:05,180
I love you, in other words, I love you.

